# 35. UI Design Direction

## Visual Identity

ARROWLOG should visually combine:

* Traditional archery
* Modern sports application
* Natural materials
* Premium competition graphics

Suggested visual language:

* Dark charcoal
* Warm sand
* Forest green
* Off-white
* Subtle bronze accents

Avoid overly futuristic/cyberpunk styling.

---

# 36. Typography

Use a modern sans-serif font.

Recommended:

* Inter
* Geist
* Plus Jakarta Sans

Headings may use a slightly condensed display font for result posters.

---

# 37. UX Principles

## Rule 1 — Shoot first, tap less

Score entry should require minimal interaction.

## Rule 2 — Big touch targets

Minimum recommended:

```text
44 × 44 px
```

Prefer:

```text
52–64 px
```

for score buttons.

## Rule 3 — Immediate feedback

After submitting:

```text
END 3 SAVED ✓
49 POINTS
```

## Rule 4 — Never lose score

Scores should persist immediately after submission.

## Rule 5 — Offline-friendly

The scoring interface should tolerate temporary network interruptions.

---

# 38. PWA Requirements

ARROWLOG must support:

* Install to Home Screen
* Mobile viewport
* Standalone mode
* App icon
* Splash screen
* Service worker
* Basic offline caching

Offline scoring architecture should be considered during implementation.

Minimum v1:

```text
Score Entry
↓
Local Queue
↓
Network Available
↓
Sync
```

If full offline synchronization is too complex for MVP, implement resilient local draft storage first.

