# 61. Phase 3

## AI Target Scanning

Upload target image.

AI detects:

* Target face
* Arrow locations
* Approximate scoring rings

User confirms.

Then:

```text
SAVE SCORES
```

AI must never automatically finalize an official score without confirmation.

---

# 62. Phase 4

## Tournament Mode

Support:

* Qualification
* Multiple rounds
* Categories
* Age groups
* Gender categories
* Elimination
* Finals
* Official result export
* Certificates

This should be designed as a separate domain layer rather than overloading the casual session model.

---

# 63. Future Monetization

Possible model:

### Free

* Personal scoring
* Basic sessions
* Basic leaderboard

### Community

* Unlimited sessions
* Custom branding
* Advanced statistics
* Result templates
* Community profile

### Tournament

* Tournament management
* Registration
* Categories
* Brackets
* Certificates
* Advanced reporting

Do not implement monetization in v1.

---

# 64. MVP Acceptance Criteria

ARROWLOG v1 is considered complete when:

### Session

* [ ] Organizer can create a session.
* [ ] Organizer can configure ends and arrows.
* [ ] Session generates unique QR code.
* [ ] Session can be opened and closed.

### Archer

* [ ] Archer can scan/join session.
* [ ] Archer can enter name.
* [ ] Archer can select bow type.
* [ ] Archer can submit scores.

### Scoring

* [ ] Score validation works.
* [ ] End total is automatically calculated.
* [ ] Session total is automatically calculated.
* [ ] Average is calculated.
* [ ] Scores persist in database.
* [ ] Organizer can edit scores.

### Leaderboard

* [ ] Leaderboard updates automatically.
* [ ] Ranking is calculated server-side.
* [ ] Ties are handled consistently.

### Results

* [ ] Completed session generates results.
* [ ] Individual result card is generated.
* [ ] Result card can be downloaded.
* [ ] Result can be shared.

### PWA

* [ ] App works on mobile.
* [ ] App can be installed.
* [ ] App icon exists.
* [ ] Basic offline resilience exists.

---

# 65. Definition of Done

A feature is considered done only when:

1. UI is implemented.
2. Mobile layout is tested.
3. Database operations work.
4. RLS policies are verified.
5. Validation exists.
6. Error states exist.
7. Loading states exist.
8. Empty states exist.
9. Data persists correctly.
10. Feature works on a real mobile device.

