# 68. Core Domain Model

```text
Community
   │
   ├── Members
   │
   └── Sessions
          │
          ├── Session Archers
          │       │
          │       └── Ends
          │              │
          │              └── Arrows
          │
          └── Results
                  │
                  └── Posters
```

---

# 69. Product Principle

The central principle of ARROWLOG:

> **The archer should spend more time shooting and less time calculating.**

Every UX decision should support this.

If a feature adds complexity without improving scoring, session management, community engagement, or result sharing, it should not be included in v1.

---

# 70. Future Product Direction

ARROWLOG should eventually become a lightweight digital platform for archery communities.

Potential ecosystem:

```text
ARROWLOG
│
├── Casual Sessions
├── Training
├── Community
├── Personal Statistics
├── Competitions
├── Tournament Mode
├── Certificates
├── AI Target Scanning
└── Social Results
```

The v1 architecture must therefore remain modular enough to support these features without rebuilding the scoring engine.

---

# 71. Final MVP Scope

The first production version should focus on one simple experience:

```text
CREATE SESSION
      ↓
SCAN QR
      ↓
ENTER ARROW SCORES
      ↓
AUTO CALCULATE
      ↓
LIVE LEADERBOARD
      ↓
FINAL RESULTS
      ↓
SHARE RESULT CARD
```

Everything else is secondary.

**ARROWLOG v1 = Digital Scorebook + Live Leaderboard + Shareable Results.**

---

# 72. Product Tagline

Primary:

> **Shoot. Score. Share.**

Alternative:

> **Your session. Your score. Your story.**

Malay alternative:

> **Panah. Kira. Kongsi.**
